## [:< ##

# name  = user-edit.form.collapse_summary_field_names
# descr = which scalar record fields collapse to a length summary when unfocused
# param = -none-

## the SAME shape user-edit.form.multiline_field_names already is, for the
## same reason -- see that module's own header for the full account of why a
## POLICY name list needs ONE shared module rather than a hand-duplicated copy
## per call site : user-edit.form.schema_from_record [ a field already present
## on a loaded record ] and user-edit.form.add_field [ a field being added for
## the FIRST time via the add-a-field cycler ] both need this list, and a
## second copy would drift exactly the way that module's header warns about.
##
## unlike multiline/list, a plain scalar field reserves NO width in user-edit.
## form.build_frame at all today -- it already resizes the frame live as text
## is typed into it, an accepted, pre-existing behaviour. per user, this stays
## unreserved rather than growing the dual-row-set machinery multiline/list
## needed : the frame can widen/narrow on focus change for a collapsing field,
## same as it already does while typing into any ordinary field, without a
## visible correctness problem being reported.
##
## 'host_password' [ masked type ] is safe here specifically because render_
## form passes the already-RANDOMIZED display value into editor.control.
## scalar.summary, not the real one -- the count shown is the star total, not
## the real character count [ editor.control.get_display_value's variable
## star-count-per-character note ]. would have been a straight length leak
## before that existed.
##
## EXTEND HERE alongside users.record.optional_fields and user-edit.form.
## multiline_field_names -- adding a new collapsing field costs one word here.

return qw| full_real_name location host_password |;

